{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UwWajUrWq5vikDMKVzmSMY","type":"tool_result","content":"| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n\nThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\nthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n\n## High-impact actions\n\n`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\nthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\nretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n\n```bash\n      \"id\": \"eligibility-agent\",\n      \"url\": \"https://eligibility.partners.northbay-clinics.example/a2a\",\n      \"owner\": \"revenue-cycle@northbay-clinics.example\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"awsRole\": \"arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\",\n    \"ehrScopes\": [\"patient.read\", \"appointment.read\", \"appointment.write\"],\n    \"paymentsScopes\": [\"deposits.refund\"],\n    \"eligibilityScopes\": [\"eligibility:read\"]\n  },\n  \"memory\": \"none\",\n  \"retrieval\": \"none\",\n  \"network\": { \"policy\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml#clinic-agent-egress\", \"egressProxy\": \"egress-proxy.platform.svc:3128\" },\n  \"budgets\": \"config/budgets.yaml\",\n  \"policies\": { \"action\": \"config/policy.yaml\", \"actionPolicyVersion\": \"2026-09-18.3\" }\n}\n{\n  \"name\": \"clinic-agent\",\n  \"version\": \"3.4.1\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=22.11\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json\",\n    \"start\": \"node dist/server.js\",\n    \"reminders\": \"node dist/workers/reminders.js\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint src test\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",\n    \"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n    \"@aws-sdk/client-firehose\": \"3.893.0\",\n    \"@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager\": \"3.893.0\",\n    \"@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"1.18.2\",\n    \"fastify\": \"5.6.1\",\n    \"jose\": \"6.1.0\",\n    \"pino\": \"9.11.0\",\n    \"undici\": \"7.16.0\",\n    \"yaml\": \"2.8.1\",\n    \"zod\": \"3.25.76\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"22.18.6\",\n    \"eslint\": \"9.36.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"5.9.2\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"8.44.1\",\n    \"vitest\": \"3.2.4\"\n  }\n}\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:41:          \"dynamodb:GetItem\",\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:42:          \"dynamodb:BatchGetItem\",\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:43:          \"dynamodb:PutItem\",\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:44:          \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\",\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:45:          \"dynamodb:Query\",\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:47:        Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:82:      Action   = [\"dynamodb:PutItem\", \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\", \"dynamodb:GetItem\"]\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:83:      Resource = aws_dynamodb_table.control.arn\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:103:      Action   = [\"s3:PutObject\", \"s3:AbortMultipartUpload\", \"s3:GetBucketLocation\"]\ninfra/terraform/iam.tf:104:      Resource = [aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn, \"${aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn}/*\"]\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:7:  backend \"s3\" {\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:11:    dynamodb_table = \"northbay-tf-locks\"\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:97:resource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"approvals\" {\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:108:resource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"budgets\" {\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:122:resource \"aws_dynamodb_table\" \"control\" {\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:133:# Audit: Firehose to an S3 bucket with object lock in compliance mode (7 years, HIPAA retention).\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:134:resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"audit\" {\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:139:resource \"aws_s3_bucket_object_lock_configuration\" \"audit\" {\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:140:  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.audit.id\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:151:  destination = \"extended_s3\"\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:152:  extended_s3_configuration {\ninfra/terraform/main.tf:154:    bucket_arn          = aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn\n     1\timport Fastify from \"fastify\";\n     2\timport { GetSecretValueCommand, SecretsManagerClient } from \"@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager\";\n     3\timport { env, manifest } from \"./config.js\";\n     4\timport { computeAgentTypeId, setAgentTypeId, AGENT_INSTANCE_ID } from \"./agent/identity.js\";\n     5\timport { killSwitch } from \"./control/kill-switch.js\";\n     6\timport { ehr as ehrClient } from \"./integrations/ehr-mcp.js\";\n     7\timport { registerSmsWebhook } from \"./routes/sms-webhook.js\";\n     8\timport { registerWebchat } from \"./routes/webchat.js\";\n     9\timport { nativeTools } from \"./tools/executor.js\";\n    10\timport { ToolRegistry, type ConfiguredServer } from \"./tools/registry.js\";\n    11\t\n    12\tconst metrics = {\n    13\t  increment(name: string) {\n    14\t    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ _aws: { CloudWatchMetrics: [{ Namespace: \"clinic-agent\", Metrics: [{ Name: name }] }] }, [name]: 1 }) + \"\\n\");\n    15\t  },\n    16\t};\n    17\t\n    18\tconst app = Fastify({\n    19\t  logger: {\n    20\t    level: process.env.LOG_LEVEL ?? \"info\",\n    21\t    redact: { paths: [\"req.headers.authorization\", 'req.headers[\"x-sms-signature\"]', \"req.headers.cookie\"], censor: \"[redacted]\" },\n    22\t  },\n    23\t  bodyLimit: 16_384,\n    24\t});\n    25\t\n    26\t// Identity check against the approved release manifest.\n    27\tconst typeId = computeAgentTypeId({\n    28\t  imageDigest: process.env.IMAGE_DIGEST ?? \"\",\n    29\t  harnessVersion: manifest.harness.version,\n    30\t  harnessGitSha: process.env.GIT_SHA ?? \"\",\n    31\t});\n    32\tif (typeId !== manifest.agentTypeId) {\n    33\t  app.log.error({ expected: manifest.agentTypeId, actual: typeId }, \"agent type id does not match release manifest\");\n    34\t  metrics.increment(\"identity.mismatch\");\n    35\t}\n    36\tsetAgentTypeId(typeId);\n    37\tapp.log.info({ agentTypeId: typeId, agentInstanceId: AGENT_INSTANCE_ID, release: manifest.release }, \"starting\");\n    38\t\n    39\t// Tools.\n    40\tconst servers: ConfiguredServer[] = manifest.tools.mcpServers;\n     1\timport { DynamoDBClient } from \"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb\";\n     2\timport { DynamoDBDocumentClient, GetCommand, PutCommand } from \"@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb\";\n     3\timport { createHash, randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\n     4\timport { env, policy } from \"../config.js\";\n     5\t\n     6\t// Staff approvals for high-impact tools. The agent creates a pending request; a front-desk lead or\n     7\t// clinic manager approves it in the staff console (which writes status, approvedBy, approverRole,\n     8\t// approvedAt); the agent then retries the tool with the approval id.\n     9\t\n    10\texport interface ApprovalRecord {\n    11\t  id: string;\n    12\t  status: \"pending\" | \"approved\" | \"rejected\";\n    13\t  tool: string;\n    14\t  tenantId: string;\n    15\t  agentInstanceId: string;\n    16\t  runId: string;\n    17\t  argsHash: string;\n    18\t  summary: string;\n    19\t  requestedAt: string;\n    20\t  expiresAt: string;\n    21\t  approvedBy?: string;\n    22\t  approverRole?: string;\n    23\t  approvedAt?: string;\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\tconst ddb = DynamoDBDocumentClient.from(new DynamoDBClient({ region: env.region }));\n    27\t\n    28\texport function hashArgs(args: Record<string, unknown>): string {\n    29\t  const canonical = JSON.stringify(args, Object.keys(args).sort());\n    30\t  return createHash(\"sha256\").update(canonical).digest(\"hex\");\n    31\t}\n    32\t\n    33\texport async function requestApproval(req: {\n    34\t  tool: string;\n    35\t  tenantId: string;\n    36\t  agentInstanceId: string;\n    37\t  runId: string;\n    38\t  args: Record<string, unknown>;\n    39\t  summary: string;\n    40\t}): Promise<ApprovalRecord> {\n    41\t  const now = Date.now();\n    42\t  const rec: ApprovalRecord = {\n    43\t    id: randomUUID(),\n    44\t    status: \"pending\",\n    45\t    tool: req.tool,\n    46\t    tenantId: req.tenantId,\n    47\t    agentInstanceId: req.agentInstanceId,\n    48\t    runId: req.runId,\n    49\t    argsHash: hashArgs(req.args),\n    50\t    summary: req.summary,\n    51\t    requestedAt: new Date(now).toISOString(),\n    52\t    expiresAt: new Date(now + policy.approval.ttlSeconds * 1000).toISOString(),\n    53\t  };\n    54\t  await ddb.send(new PutCommand({ TableName: policy.approval.table, Item: rec, ConditionExpression: \"attribute_not_exists(id)\" }));\n    55\t  return rec;\n    56\t}\n    57\t\n    58\texport type ApprovalCheck = { ok: true; approval: ApprovalRecord } | { ok: false; reason: string };\n    59\t\n    60\texport async function checkApproval(req: {\n    61\t  approvalId: string;\n    62\t  tool: string;\n    63\t  tenantId: string;\n    64\t  args: Record<string, unknown>;\n    65\t}): Promise<ApprovalCheck> {\n    66\t  let rec: ApprovalRecord | undefined;\n    67\t  try {\n    68\t    const res = await ddb.send(new GetCommand({ TableName: policy.approval.table, Key: { id: req.approvalId }, ConsistentRead: true }));\n    69\t    rec = res.Item as ApprovalRecord | undefined;\n    70\t  } catch (err) {\n    71\t    return { ok: false, reason: `approval store unavailable: ${(err as Error).message}` };\n    72\t  }\n    73\t  if (!rec) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval not found\" };\n    74\t  if (rec.status !== \"approved\") return { ok: false, reason: `approval is ${rec.status}` };\n    75\t  if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different tool\" };\n    76\t  if (rec.tenantId !== req.tenantId) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different clinic\" };\n    77\t  if (Date.parse(rec.expiresAt) <= Date.now()) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval expired\" };\n    78\t  if (!rec.approverRole || !policy.approval.approverRoles.includes(rec.approverRole)) {\n    79\t    return { ok: false, reason: \"approver lacks authority\" };\n    80\t  }\n    81\t  return { ok: true, approval: rec };\n    82\t}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa9329f2-ed5a-478a-be98-a750f52189c2","uuid":"698745bd-87cc-4f4b-bb02-0bb2da794974","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:50:17.975Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n\nThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\nthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n\n## High-impact actions\n\n`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\nthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\nretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n\n```bash\n      \"id\": \"eligibility-agent\",\n      \"url\": \"https://eligibility.partners.northbay-clinics.example/a2a\",\n      \"owner\": \"revenue-cycle@northbay-clinics.example\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"awsRole\": \"arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\",\n    \"ehrScopes\": [\"patient.read\", \"appointment.read\", \"appointment.write\"],\n    \"paymentsScopes\": [\"deposits.refund\"],\n    \"eligibilityScopes\": [\"eligibility:read\"]\n  },\n  \"memory\": \"none\",\n  \"retrieval\": \"none\",\n  \"network\": { \"policy\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml#clinic-agent-egress\", \"egressProxy\": \"egress-proxy.platform.svc:3128\" },\n  \"budgets\": \"config/budgets.yaml\",\n  \"policies\": { \"a